{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================================
  GOD SQUAD — verse-feature.liquid

  BAND 1 of the Verse feature: the "Today's Verse" strip. Three panels in one
  row — a cream verse panel, a photograph, and an ink message panel — collapsing
  to a single column on a phone.

  Sources of truth: the owner's approved Verse mockup for the composition,
  PHASE-2-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md for every colour, type role and spacing rung, and
  sections/our-story.liquid for the house style this file follows.

  THE PHOTOGRAPH IS A SETTING, NOT AN ASSET. The ten JPEGs in
  brand-assets/verse images/ are crops of a flattened mockup screenshot — their
  own README says any typography baked into the screenshot survives in the crop,
  and it does: the card crops carry their own quote and link painted into the
  pixels. None of them can ship. The merchant supplies the photograph.

  NO DERIVED HEADING LEVEL. our-story.liquid and featured-collection.liquid both
  compute a child heading level because they emit repeated headings beneath a
  clearable h2. This band does not: the quote is a blockquote, the eyebrow and
  the caption are labels, and nothing here heads a subsection. One h2, no h3.
  ============================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign img = section.settings.image
  assign img_mobile = section.settings.mobile_image

  assign eyebrow = section.settings.eyebrow | strip
  assign reference = section.settings.reference | strip
  assign quote = section.settings.quote | strip
  assign caption = section.settings.caption | strip
  assign message_eyebrow = section.settings.message_eyebrow | strip
  assign link_label = section.settings.link_label | strip
  assign link_url = section.settings.link_url

  assign surface_class = 'surface-light'
  if section.settings.surface == 'dark'
    assign surface_class = 'surface-dark'
  endif

  comment
    The reflection link follows hero.liquid's rule exactly: a label alone is not
    a control. No reflection page exists yet, so shipping the label with no
    destination would put a dead link on the home page; it stays hidden until
    the merchant gives it somewhere to go, and the editor notice says so.
  endcomment
  assign show_link = false
  if link_label != blank and link_url != blank
    assign show_link = true
  endif

  comment
    The message panel earns its ink ground only when it has something in it.
    An empty inverse panel is a black rectangle beside a photograph.
  endcomment
  assign show_message = false
  if section.settings.message != blank or message_eyebrow != blank or show_link
    assign show_message = true
  endif

  comment
    Three panels at the widest, so the photograph is roughly a third of the
    viewport; one column below that, where it is the full width.
  endcomment
  assign img_sizes = '(min-width: 1280px) 40vw, 100vw'

  assign classes = 'verse-feature '
  assign classes = classes | append: surface_class
  assign classes = classes | append: ' verse-feature--pt-' | append: section.settings.spacing_top
  assign classes = classes | append: ' verse-feature--pb-' | append: section.settings.spacing_bottom
  if show_message
    assign classes = classes | append: ' verse-feature--has-message'
  endif
  comment
    The media modifier is unconditional now: the panel always has a photograph,
    either the merchant's or the bundled stand-in, so the three-panel layout
    this class selects is always the correct one.
  endcomment
  assign classes = classes | append: ' verse-feature--has-media'
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  A band with no verse and no photograph has nothing to say, so on the live
  storefront it renders nothing. In the Theme Editor it always renders, with a
  note naming what is missing. Same guard as our-story.liquid:125.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if reference == blank and quote == blank and img == blank and request.design_mode == false -%}
  {%- comment -%} Not configured yet: render nothing, and request nothing. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- else -%}

{{ 'section-verse-feature.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<div class="{{ classes }}" {% if section.settings.anchor_id != blank %}id="{{ section.settings.anchor_id | handle }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="verse-feature__row">

    {%- comment -%} ------------------------------------------ the verse panel {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="verse-feature__panel verse-feature__panel--verse">
      {%- if eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="verse-feature__eyebrow">{{ eyebrow | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if reference != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          An h2, never an h1 — the home page's single h1 belongs to the hero.
          The reference is the heading because it is what the band is about.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <h2 class="verse-feature__reference">{{ reference | escape | newline_to_br }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if quote != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          A blockquote, because it is a quotation, and cite on the element
          carries the source for anything parsing the page. The line break is
          the merchant's: newline_to_br, so the two-line setting in the mockup
          breaks where they typed it rather than where the box happens to end.
          escape runs BEFORE newline_to_br — reversed, the <br> would be eaten.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <blockquote class="verse-feature__quote">
          <p>{{ quote | escape | newline_to_br }}</p>
        </blockquote>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if caption != blank -%}
        <p class="verse-feature__caption">{{ caption | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ------------------------------------------------ the photo {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="verse-feature__media">
      {%- if img != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Alt text is the merchant's, set on the image in Shopify admin, and is
          never invented here — the theme cannot know what is in the photograph.
          Empty alt announces it as decorative, which is correct for a mood
          photograph beside a quote that already carries the message.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if img_mobile != blank -%}
          <picture>
            <source
              media="(max-width: 1279px)"
              srcset="
                {{ img_mobile | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w,
                {{ img_mobile | image_url: width: 640 }} 640w,
                {{ img_mobile | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w,
                {{ img_mobile | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w,
                {{ img_mobile | image_url: width: 1500 }} 1500w,
                {{ img_mobile | image_url: width: 2048 }} 2048w
              "
              sizes="100vw"
              width="{{ img_mobile.width }}"
              height="{{ img_mobile.height }}"
            >
            {{
              img
              | image_url: width: 2400
              | image_tag:
                class: 'verse-feature__image',
                widths: '480, 640, 900, 1200, 1500, 1800, 2100, 2400',
                sizes: img_sizes,
                loading: 'lazy',
                decoding: 'async',
                alt: img.alt
            }}
          </picture>
        {%- else -%}
          {{
            img
            | image_url: width: 2400
            | image_tag:
              class: 'verse-feature__image',
              widths: '480, 640, 900, 1200, 1500, 1800, 2100, 2400',
              sizes: img_sizes,
              loading: 'lazy',
              decoding: 'async',
              alt: img.alt
          }}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {% render 'image-fallback',
          file: 'hero.webp',
          class: 'verse-feature__image',
          sizes: img_sizes,
          width: 1672,
          height: 941
        %}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ---------------------------------------- the message panel {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if show_message -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        surface-dark nested inside the band re-declares all five context
        variables at this scope, which is Phase 2 operating rule 3: an inverse
        block is a nested surface class, never an override of individual colour
        properties. That is the path that produces gold on cream.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="verse-feature__panel verse-feature__panel--message surface-dark">
        {%- if message_eyebrow != blank -%}
          <p class="verse-feature__eyebrow">{{ message_eyebrow | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.message != blank -%}
          <div class="verse-feature__message rte">{{ section.settings.message }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if show_link -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            The arrow is the theme's own snippet, not a literal → glyph. Phase 2
            section 10.4 records why: Jost carries neither U+2192 nor U+20B1, so
            the character falls back to a per-platform face and its weight and
            baseline move between devices. It is aria-hidden inside the snippet,
            because the label already says where the link goes.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <a class="verse-feature__link" href="{{ link_url }}">
            {{ link_label | escape }}
            {% render 'icon-arrow', class: 'icon--sm' %}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- if request.design_mode -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign notices = ''
      if img == blank
        assign notices = notices | append: 'no_image|'
      elsif img.alt == blank
        assign notices = notices | append: 'no_alt|'
      endif
      if link_label != blank and link_url == blank
        assign notices = notices | append: 'no_link_url|'
      endif
    -%}
    {%- if notices != blank -%}
      <div class="verse-feature__notice">
        {%- if notices contains 'no_image' -%}
          <p>{{ 'sections.verse_feature.no_image' | t }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if notices contains 'no_alt' -%}
          <p>{{ 'sections.verse_feature.no_alt' | t }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if notices contains 'no_link_url' -%}
          <p>{{ 'sections.verse_feature.no_link_url' | t }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Today's Verse",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "verse-feature-section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Verse"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "Today's Verse"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "reference",
      "label": "Reference",
      "info": "The book, chapter and verse. Shown as the band's heading.",
      "default": "2 Corinthians 5:7"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "quote",
      "label": "Verse",
      "info": "Line breaks are kept, so the quote breaks where you type it.",
      "default": "“For we walk by faith,\nnot by sight.”"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "caption",
      "label": "Caption",
      "default": "Walk By Faith."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Photograph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "Image",
      "info": "Set alt text on the image itself in Content > Files, so screen readers describe it."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "mobile_image",
      "label": "Mobile image",
      "info": "Optional. A taller crop for narrow screens. The main image is used when this is empty."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "The message"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "message_eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "The Message"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "message",
      "label": "Message",
      "default": "<p>Faith means moving forward even when the destination isn't completely visible.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "link_label",
      "label": "Link label",
      "default": "Read Full Reflection"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "link_url",
      "label": "Link",
      "info": "The link stays hidden until this is set, so the band never ships a link to nothing."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "surface",
      "label": "Surface",
      "info": "Phase 2 allows a home page two surface changes. This band is the third if it differs from the one above it.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "light", "label": "Cream" },
        { "value": "dark", "label": "Ink" }
      ],
      "default": "light"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "spacing_top",
      "label": "Space above",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "None" },
        { "value": "tight", "label": "Tight" },
        { "value": "standard", "label": "Standard" }
      ],
      "default": "standard"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "spacing_bottom",
      "label": "Space below",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "None" },
        { "value": "tight", "label": "Tight" },
        { "value": "standard", "label": "Standard" }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "anchor_id",
      "label": "Anchor",
      "info": "Lets a menu item link to this band with #verse.",
      "default": "verse"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Today's Verse",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Today's Verse",
        "reference": "2 Corinthians 5:7",
        "quote": "“For we walk by faith,\nnot by sight.”",
        "caption": "Walk By Faith.",
        "message_eyebrow": "The Message",
        "message": "<p>Faith means moving forward even when the destination isn't completely visible.</p>",
        "link_label": "Read Full Reflection",
        "surface": "light",
        "spacing_top": "standard",
        "spacing_bottom": "none",
        "anchor_id": "verse"
      }
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
